<article class="env-lemma" id="01AX">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/01AX">Lemma <span data-tag="01AX">17.6.1</span>.</a> Let $X$ be a topological space. Let $Z \subset X$ be a closed subset. Denote $i : Z \to X$ the inclusion map. The functor </p>
  <div class="equation">
  \[  i_* : \textit{Ab}(Z) \longrightarrow \textit{Ab}(X)  \]
</div>
  <p> is exact, fully faithful, with essential image exactly those abelian sheaves whose support is contained in $Z$. The functor $i^{-1}$ is a left inverse to $i_*$. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      Exactness follows from the description of stalks in Sheaves, Lemma <a href="/tag/00AE" data-tag="00AE">6.32.1</a> and Lemma <a href="/tag/01AG" data-tag="01AG">17.3.1</a>. The rest was shown in Sheaves, Lemma <a href="/tag/00AG" data-tag="00AG">6.32.3</a>. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>